1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,538
A: What if a looped Transformer used RWKV-7 as its recurrent mixer, instead of GDN?

2
00:00:07,538 --> 00:00:14,000
B: That sounds like a small code change with a big architectural question.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,304
A: First, the relation. A Universal Transformer reuses the same transition block across depth steps.

4
00:00:21,304 --> 00:00:28,087
B: So a looped Transformer is the language-model version of that same recurrence idea?

5
00:00:28,087 --> 00:00:33,043
A: Exactly. It repeatedly applies a shared Transformer block.

6
00:00:33,043 --> 00:00:38,000
LT2 asks what efficient token mixer should live inside that loop.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,263
A: Each loop pass adds effective computation without adding a new copy of the parameters.

8
00:00:44,263 --> 00:00:49,184
B: The shared block sees the updated hidden state again and again.

9
00:00:49,184 --> 00:00:55,000
A: Right. The attraction is more recurrent refinement at nearly the same model size.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:03,140
A: The LT2 baseline uses GDN, a DPLR-style recurrent mixer.

11
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:11,279
I added a full RWKV-7 native block, with time mix and channel mix, as its replacement.

12
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:17,140
B: Same looping idea, but a more expressive recurrent core.

13
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:23,000
A: In the repo, the switch is `layer_pattern = "rwkv7_native"`.

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,043
A: Then I ran a parameter-matched real-token test on FineWeb sp ten twenty-four.

15
00:01:30,043 --> 00:01:32,391
B: Nearly the same parameters?

16
00:01:32,391 --> 00:01:40,609
A: Yes. GDN has nine hundred sixty-two thousand parameters; RWKV-7 has nine hundred fifty-nine thousand.

17
00:01:40,609 --> 00:01:50,000
B: And RWKV-7 reached about one point five seven times the throughput, with lower final validation loss.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,561
A: Look at the smoothed training curve.

19
00:01:54,561 --> 00:01:59,122
In this five-thousand-step ablation, RWKV-7 drops faster and stays below GDN.

20
00:01:59,122 --> 00:02:05,561
B: It is still an early small-scale run, not the final pretraining verdict.

21
00:02:05,561 --> 00:02:12,000
A: Correct. But it is a strong reason to run the full comparison.

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:22,960
A: The hypothesis is simple: looping already benefits recurrent mixers, and RWKV-7 may be a better recurrent core for LT2.

23
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:33,920
B: Give RWKV-7 a try. The code and curve are at github dot com slash xiaol slash LT2 dash RWKV.
